@startuml server_release_happy
title MongoDB Server (mongo / SERVER) — Release (Happy Path)

skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFF6E5
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #B8860B
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3CD
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F5F5F5

' Legend:
'   |Human|  = Eng / Release Mgr (manual step / decision)
'   |CI|     = Evergreen CI / Copybara (automated)

' Lane order is set by first appearance: declare CI first so it renders on the left.
|CI|
|Human|
start

:work lands on **master** (private 10gen/mongo);

' Comment 4 + 8: branches are long-lived, cut only ~1-2x/year off master,
' NOT once per release. A vX.Y lives until the version is EOL.
if (new major/minor line needed? (~1-2x per year)) then (yes)
  :**BRANCH CUT** — create **vX.Y** + **vX.Y-staging**
  new Evergreen project mongodb-mongo-vX.Y
  branch is long-lived: supported until version EOL
  (e.g. v8.0 cut 2024, supported to 2029+);
  note right
    Most releases REUSE an existing supported
    branch — no branch cut. EOL lines (e.g. v4.4)
    are only touched during emergency responses.
  end note
else (no — reuse existing supported branch)
endif

:engineers open PRs to **vX.Y-staging** (integration);

:**MANAGER promotes** vX.Y-staging -> **vX.Y** (production)
[human APPROVAL GATE];

:tag **rX.Y.Z-rcN** (push git tag);

|CI|
partition "RC BUILD (Evergreen)" {
  :add git tag -> stamp MONGO_VERSION (strips leading 'r');
  :compile (release variants);
  :package -> DEB / RPM / MSI / tarball;
  :sign -> garasign (GPG / jsign MSI);
  :push -> upload signed artifacts to the release bucket
  (RC-versioned; not listed on the Downloads page yet)
  skip_existing guards protect already-shipped artifacts;
  note right
    publish_packages/push also run on the release-branch
    waterfall at RC time (is_release is true for -rcN), but
    RC builds are not surfaced on the Downloads page.
  end note
}

:**test the RC** (correctness / perf / multiversion);

|Human|
' Comment 6: reworded from "green AND no open release blockers"
if (manually verified: no frightening build failures\nAND critical fixes complete?) then (yes)
  :tag **rX.Y.Z** (GA — un-suffixed tag)
  [human GA PROMOTION GATE];
else (no)
  :re-spin rc(N+1), or hold -> see unhappy-path diagram;
  stop
endif

|CI|
partition "GA BUILD (Evergreen)" {
  :add git tag -> stamp X.Y.Z;
  :compile · package · sign · push (internal artifacts);
}

' Comments 7, 9, 12: correct ordering is
' Atlas -> OM/CM -> Downloads/publish_packages -> Copybara (last).
partition "ATLAS ROLLOUT" {
  :version manifest merged · AVM / PVM rollout on **Atlas**;
}

if (Atlas rollout successful?) then (yes)
  partition "OM / CM" {
    :OM / CM release support for the new GA version;
  }

  partition "DOWNLOADS (very end)" {
    :publish_packages -> curator/barque submits to repo.mongodb.org
    + the GA version is listed on the **Downloads page**;
  }

  ' A partition must not span swimlanes — PlantUML renders one empty frame per
  ' extra lane. Close it before switching back to |CI|.
  |Human|
  partition "PUBLIC RELEASE (Copybara)" {
    :enable the release-tag mirror — PR to **10gen/mongo**
    adding/enabling a sync_tag(rX.Y.Z) fragment
    (release-team initiated; runs ONLY after Downloads
    has the versions);
  }

  |CI|
  partition "COPYBARA SYNC" {
    :Copybara advances the public branch, then publishes
    the tag -> pushes to public **mongodb/mongo**;
    note right: Direction: 10gen/mongo (private) -> mongodb/mongo (public);\nsafety checks refuse to move the public branch backward
  }

  :**RELEASED** — X.Y.Z on Downloads + Atlas / CM / OM
  git tag = version;
  stop
else (no)
  :withhold from OM/CM + Downloads -> abandon GA
  (see unhappy-path diagram);
  stop
endif

@enduml
